# Price-loop diagnosis plan

## Goal

Finish one end-to-end daily PIT price/volume replay and identify the smallest
engine change needed to avoid missing otherwise-valid CANSLIM entries.

## Global constraints

- Use only the existing local PIT bundle and normalized artifacts.
- Do not download or reprocess SEC/13F data.
- Do not touch the optimizer, live/paper execution, or shared branches.
- CANSLIM fidelity is a hard constraint; do not weaken entry thresholds.
- Do not add tests until the build is finished, per user direction.
- Any code change must preserve causal as-of behavior and be verified with one
  bounded replay.

## Tasks

1. Audit daily cadence, same-day volume gating, and PIT price coverage using
   bounded read-only runs.
2. Implement the smallest evidence-backed engine change, if one is required,
   using a fresh implementer and a scoped review.
3. Run a bounded daily replay and reconcile signals, executions, cash, and
   artifacts.
